// Selenium Python — Sphinx API-listing codegen.
//
// Drives `generate_api_module_listing.py`, which recursively walks
// the `selenium/` package directory and writes
// `docs/source/api.rst` (the master listing Sphinx's autogen feeds
// into for the Python API docs).
//
// The script takes no CLI args. Upstream Selenium runs it via
// `bazel run //py:generate_api_module_listing` (a Bazel-shaped
// py_binary with default-runfiles). The aeb shape is a
// `python.codegen(b)` block declaring the input directory tree and
// the single output file.
//
// **Why this leaf exists and was deferred until now:** the AEB
// migration status doc listed it as gap-not-closed because the
// upstream script's inputs are "every .py under selenium/" with no
// explicit declared input. The bridge `python.codegen` provides is
// the `codegen_input_dir(dir)` setter — declare a tree, every file
// in it counts toward the staleness check (recursively, via
// `_dir_newest_mtime` in lib/python). Now any change inside
// `selenium/` invalidates `api.rst`; the script re-runs on the next
// build; outputs are verified for existence.
//
// Note on staleness model: this is NOT hermetic — the script also
// does `import site` and reads installed-package metadata. If the
// venv changes underneath without `selenium/` changing on disk,
// staleness won't notice. The reasonable answer is "if you change
// the venv, delete the api.rst output." The same is true of the
// PyTorch torchgen leaf and most codegen tools that reach outside
// their declared inputs.

import bldr
import python
import python (codegen_script, codegen_input_dir, codegen_output)

main() {
    b = bldr.start()

    python.codegen(b) {
        codegen_script("generate_api_module_listing.py")

        // Recursive walk of selenium/ feeds the staleness check.
        // Every .py file under here participates in the mtime
        // comparison via `_dir_newest_mtime`.
        codegen_input_dir("selenium")

        // The single declared output. python.codegen fails the
        // build if this file doesn't exist after the script runs.
        codegen_output("docs/source/api.rst")
    }
}
